Lars Pastewka and Mark O. Robbins. *When are rough surfaces sticky?*, [arXiv:1311.1178v1, 5 November 2013](https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.1178v1) · [26-page manuscript with supplementary material](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1311.1178v1). The archive identifies the subsequent journal article as PNAS 111, 3298 (2014), [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1320846111). Keep the manuscript version distinct from the journal edition.

Read the full argument, methods and supplement. Compare its treatment of interacting rough contacts and finite attraction range with independent-asperity approximations. Reconstruct a stated prediction before applying it to another surface.

The title, early derivation, methods and selected supplementary interaction-range passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The simulations, figures and full supplement were not reproduced. The archive's [non-exclusive distribution licence](https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html) grants rights to arXiv; it is not a general adaptation licence for readers. Link this freely readable manuscript without bundling its media.

